<p>We discussed this in IRC. Log follows:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Note: Unrelated conversation removed</p>
<blockquote>
<p>17:23 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; CurtisSnyder: tell me about your idea.<br />
17:25 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Oh sorry for DMing you, I should have waited<br />
17:29 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; MalyceGraves So the idea is centered around a dishwasher that had been given to the SCP foundation, the dishwasher cleans things with tongues that protrude from the inner part of it, it also has a memetic affect on people with a slightly higher IQ, once they are within 5 meters of the SCP and know about it's anomalous properties, they become<br />
17:29 hysterical, denying that it has any anomalous properties at all. They deny any recording footage given to them or x-rays. The only way to &quot;prove&quot; that it isn't anomalous is by inserting themselves into the dishwasher, they will break their own bones if need be and nothing can stop this affect from happening, not separation, antimemetcs, even death.<br />
17:29 I want it to be a neutralized SCP so I can set up a larger story about a conflict between the 05 and the ethics committee<br />
17:31 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; CurtisSnyder: Well, you certainly got the weird part<br />
17:31 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Haha, I was hoping you'd say something along those lines<br />
17:32 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; So, it's compulsory? The people with &quot;slightly higher&quot; IQs then proceed to try and kill themselves if they read about it?<br />
17:34 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; MalyceGraves Essentially, more of a &quot;I have to see it to believe it SCP&quot;<br />
17:34 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; So what is the conflict between the O5s and EC?<br />
17:38 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; MalyceGraves So the SCP is actually suppose to pose a major threat to the foundation, a lot of foundation members (in my opinion) have to be smart in order to be apart of the foundation. The conflict starts when this relatively Euclid SCP could be contained without any hazard as long as smart people don't go near it. Well someone who is being set<br />
17:38 up to replace someone in the 05 dies to this SCP, so the 05 vote for the SCP to be destroyed. The EC doesn't want that as it can be contained easily. It's basically a look at how the EC thinks the 05 are abusing their power too much and they want to stop it or make a change.<br />
17:39 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; I'm hoping that after writing some more tales and other SCP's that are connected to this SCP and follow a trend of the 05 &quot;abusing&quot; their power, it will lead to a 001 proposal<br />
17:40 I have no idea what the 001 proposal will be, that's like 3 years down the line if I even have the time<br />
17:41 I probably could have worded that conflict way better<br />
17:45 — •MalyceGraves contemplates<br />
17:46 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; CurtisSnyder: so this is intended to be a launchpad for a whole series?<br />
17:47 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Yes right now<br />
17:47 a very early launchpad<br />
17:47 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; I want to collaborate with people before I even consider starting a set story line<br />
17:48 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; MalyceGraves: The SCP I'm writing deserves a Euclid tag however because it has killed someone who was being groomed to replace an 05 member, the 05 destroyed it. The EC is saying that this SCP shouldn't be neutralized at all as it can be easily contained, all you need are people with average IQ. So this is the starting of the conflict, eventually I<br />
17:48 want the EC to start going behind the 05's back, maybe the next SCP they want neutralized is actually transported somewhere and is safe and sound, being contained by a mobile task force of some type. This will end with a 001 proposal with the 05 and the EC. Some type of agreement or some type of truth. I'm not sure what yet. (Sorry I had re-written<br />
17:48 the conflict to make it seem more interesting)<br />
17:51 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; CurtisSnyder: Ok, I want to narrow in on one aspect first. I'm not all that much of a fan of using IQ as an arbitrary dividing line between who is affected and who isn't by this thing. IQ itself is measurable by a wide variety of often inherently flawed metrics and isn't really that good at indicating who is &quot;smart&quot; and who isn't. Intellect itself is fluid and complex, so focusing on this could inevitably lead to your<br />
17:51 having to define who is and is not considered &quot;smart&quot;<br />
17:52 That can lead to complications that I'm not entirely certain you want.<br />
17:53 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; IQ is fairly arbitrary in and of itself and appears to fluctuate a great deal across the spectrum of one's life. The idea of a weird SCP being the subject of conflict between the O5 Council and EC isn't a bad one, it's been done before<br />
17:54 I've explored conflict between the two myself, actually<br />
17:54 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; I'm down to change what the dividing line is, I'd like to make it interesting and hard to detect. I also want it to be (theoretically) able to kill an 05 member under the right circumstances. Did you have a suggestion on what that dividing line could be?<br />
18:00 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; MalyceGraves: I'm down to change what the dividing line is, I'd like to make it interesting and hard to detect. I also want it to be (theoretically) able to kill an 05 member under the right circumstances. Did you have a suggestion on what that dividing line could be?<br />
18:01 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; CurtisSnyder: Most of the various dividing lines would be fairly discriminatory in nature and could open various problems you probably dont want to explore. I suggest using something fairly simple. &quot;People born on Tuesday&quot; or &quot;people between the ages of 17-28&quot;<br />
18:01 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; and by &quot;an 05&quot; I mean &quot;all 05&quot;<br />
18:01 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; The story you're telling isn't about the anomaly, but about the conflict surrounding the item. You could lock it in a box and drop it into the ocean and no one would care about it<br />
18:03 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; MalyceGraves: So you're saying that it doesn't have to be able to kill all of the 05 in order to be detrimental to The Foundation?<br />
18:04 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; The story isn't the fact that this is dangerous. For whatever reason an o5 decides to destroy it, and the EC gets pissy about it<br />
18:04 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; That's your story<br />
18:05 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Yeah, as I understand it, the EC is kind of a punching bag as The Foundation isn't known for it's proper ethics<br />
18:05 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; However, they have power and can use it<br />
18:11 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; MalyceGraves I appreciate the criticism by the way, I did have a question about the dividing line. Should their be some&#8230; explanation for why it effects the individuals it does?<br />
18:12 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; CurtisSnyder: I wouldn't focus on that overmuch. Pick a reason, make it fairly low-threat and easy to block<br />
18:12 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; MalyceGraves Do you think if I fleshed out the idea and got some more criticism, a greenlight would be possible?<br />
18:14 &lt;•MalyceGraves&gt; Give me your link<br />
18:14 Please<br />
18:15 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; MalyceGraves: I haven't asked for a greenlight yet, however if you think I should then I will. <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13897865/seeking-criticism-before-seeking-greenlight-the-perfect-dish">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/t-13897865/seeking-criticism-before-seeking-greenlight-the-perfect-dish</a></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I like the idea of the conflict between the O5s and EC. While that has been explored at some length elsewhere, it's still a concept that can be rehashed in interesting ways.</p>
<p>My takeaway from this conversation is this:</p>
<ul>
<li>Anomalous item secured by the Foundation</li>
<li>Item is anomalous and dangerous, but easily secured</li>
<li>A high level Foundation Employee is killed by it</li>
<li>The O5s use their authority to neutralize the anomaly as a result</li>
<li>The EC gets upset by what they perceive as O5 over-reach for destroying something that could have been easily contained</li>
<li>Conflict ensues.</li>
</ul>
<p>The specifics of what the anomaly is isn't what's important here. The conflict between the EC and the O5C is. The weird dishwasher with tongues is neat, I like that. Just don't use a dividing line that follows any of the usual tropes. As I said, picking something that has discriminatory baggage is probably a bad call. Use something arbitrary and innocuous like &quot;born on Tuesday&quot; or &quot;Has an Aunt with a name that starts with the letter A&quot;. Something innocuous and boring is fine, because that's not the focus here.</p>
<p>Do that, and you'll be fine. <strong><span style="color: green">Greenlight</span></strong></p>

