			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839266">
									

<p>Copy pasting this conversation for future reference. Unrelated things removed.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;the&nbsp;conversation&nbsp;log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;conversation&nbsp;log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>20:11 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; So my first concern is that the tongues part seems to be there only to weird out the reader<br />
20:15 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; My second concern is that I'm worried you're setting up too many future articles instead of focusing on developing this one<br />
20:19 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; My third concern is that you haven't specified what's the &quot;dividing line&quot;<br />
20:20 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; The tongues part is suppose to weird out the reader, it's the anomalous part. Of the SCP. Typically as a kid you see a plate that LOOKS clean however it could have just been licked by a kid. As an adult, we see a person clean a plate with their tongue and it isn't clean. Kind of like an oxymoron.<br />
20:21 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Second one is completely valid, this is actually more of a &quot;jumpstarter&quot; SCP. However I am going to put a significant amount of thought into this one and try and make it as good as I can before getting a full blown criticism on it.<br />
20:23 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; And the dividing line was originally suppose to be intelligence however after a discussion with MalyceGraves, I had decided to scrap that idea and go with something else as they had described that &quot;dividing line&quot; as &quot;too fluid&quot; or something along those lines<br />
20:23 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; I'm going to change it to something however I'm going to ponder ideas when I actually get to the writing part of the SCP<br />
20:23 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; If you have any ideas or suggestions like Malyce had, I'd really appreciate it<br />
20:23 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; I think you should make the dividing line to be something tongue-related<br />
20:24 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; Like, so the tongues have an actual purpose other than weird out the reader<br />
20:24 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; That&#8230;. is actually a really good idea<br />
20:25 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; like it knows what type of tongue or something specific about your tongue<br />
20:25 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; But you also need to make it so it mostly only targets Foundation personnel<br />
20:26 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Maybe I could make it do do with coffee?<br />
20:26 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; And the O5 Council needs to feel somewhat threatened<br />
20:26 &lt;verbaexmachina&gt; Only tongues that have been exposed to beverages from SCP-261?<br />
20:26 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Coffee is often used to relief stress<br />
20:26 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; or help with energy<br />
20:27 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Foundation personnel must drink a ton of coffee in order to help with stress or energy as SCP's take a lot of those two things to deal with them<br />
20:27 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; hmm<br />
20:28 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; I could make it about people who believe that myth about the different taste sensors on the tongue?<br />
20:28 &lt;AbsoluteSoup&gt; Maybe more generically it'd be caffeine<br />
20:28 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; I'm not sure, I feel like &quot;coffee&quot; is too ambiguous<br />
20:29 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; And the O5 needs to feel somewhat threatened by it<br />
20:29 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Saliva production? Like if you produce a certain amount of Saliva you are affected<br />
20:30 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; Maybe it has something to do with words?<br />
20:31 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; Maybe it affects people that say the word &quot;anomaly&quot; in a daily basis?<br />
20:31 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; Maybe the O5 feel like it has to do something with a GoI, so they feel threatened?<br />
20:32 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; EthanHanson could taste work?<br />
20:32 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Like if they don't like a sour tastes<br />
20:33 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; or maybe how many words people use in a day?<br />
20:33 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; maybe<br />
20:34 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; I'm just trying to think of something that could affect an 05<br />
20:35 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; Dry mouth?<br />
20:35 * EthanHanson is thinking his best<br />
20:37 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; What about if you haven't drank any water within the last hour?<br />
20:37 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; CurtisSnyder: Idk. I think I'll have to leave that up to you<br />
20:38 &lt;CurtisSnyder&gt; I'll think of something, however if you don't mind, I'll run it by you and a couple others before I actually make it the &quot;dividing line&quot;<br />
20:38 &lt;EthanHanson&gt; Yeah, it'll be best to run it buy others</p>
</blockquote>
